er corners. The hands bring their fingertips together at the center of the wet gray paver path, then separate and settle with open palms facing the distant skybridge. Charcoal storm layers gather behind the skybridge as a gray-black funnel descends, thickens into a broad rotating tornado, and develops a dusty brown-gray base across the far end of the path. Small dark fragments circle the funnel while the landscaped courtyard and glass building remain visible. Once the tornado is fully formed, the two open hands lower out of the foreground, leaving the mature funnel beneath the layered cloud canopy."},{"start":157,"end":289,"text":"A brown mound of churned soil rises at the far end of the path and lengthens along the walkway, tearing an irregular muddy gouge through the pale pavers, building a raised central ridge, and scattering dark clods and small stones along both edges. The completed long muddy gouge remains through the courtyard path while the gray-black tornado rotates ahead from its dusty ground base into the massive charcoal cloud canopy."}]}]}]}
